<<~ ahu slot=`#/heritage`>>

!! Heritage — Spider Folk

''Rank:'' Skilled (+3)  
''Effects:'' Affinity — Silk & Web; Alternate Movement — Climb; Armoured Body

!!! Affinity — Silk & Web

Tags: `[illusion] [silk] [web]`

Aki spins lines, sheets, snares, glamour scaffolds, ward webs, belay systems, ritual knots, and silk-field diagrams from web-silk.

Use this for:
* silk and web craft,
* vibration reading,
* shrine-thread omens,
* ambush geometry,
* fae-spider etiquette,
* illusion staging,
* alchemical binding.

!!! Alternate Movement — Climb

Aki climbs at normal Speed.

After 30 minutes of continuous climbing, mark Heritage and make a Wear and Tear attrition save. While marked, make another attrition save every 10 minutes of continued alternate movement.

!!! Armoured Body

Aki's true chitin grants ''+1 Armor'' and ''+1 Ward''. This comes from her body, not worn gear.

This stacks with Ichi when worn, because Heritage Armoured Body comes from the operator's form rather than equipment.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/traits`>>

!! Traits — Five Named Traits plus Hallmark Allocation

| Trait | Rank | Classification / Use |
|---|---:|---|
| Wizard | +3 | Wizard / Power skill: casting, magical analysis, hostile glamours, noospheric pressure |
| Alchemist | +3 (provisional) | Background / Path-Magic: substance preparation, transmutation, cultivation, extraction, stabilization, potions |
| Priestess | +3 (provisional) | Background / Path-Magic: shrine rites, purification, blessings, taboo law, offerings, bindings and ritual coordination |
| Mind Palace | +3 | Memorize Powers equal to Level without consuming inventory: two at Level 2 |
| Exuberant | +3 | Each Life point spent to pay for Powers counts double |
| Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine | — | Hallmark: proposed one Trait slot, subject to final accounting and progression review |

''Working Trait Inventory:'' 7 + Thought 3 = 10 slots. Five named Traits occupy five; assign the shrine Hallmark to a sixth Trait slot only as the current working allocation. Thus ''6/10 in use; 4 open'' if that assignment holds. Spider Folk Heritage rides free under FTLS.

!!! Annotation — Split Backgrounds (RULING)

The old combined Alchemist Priestess +3 entry split into distinct ''Alchemist'' and ''Priestess'' Background Traits, each functioning as ''Path-Magic'' (also called Half-Magic). The source combined entry recorded +3 only once; independently granting each +3 remains an explicit ''provisional rank'', not a documented XP purchase. These Backgrounds grant relevant skill and trained minor workings, not unrestricted Full Powers.

!!! Annotation — Path-Magic Scope (RULING; numeric crafting procedure OPEN)

Alchemist understands the magical/material affordances of reagents, including compatible excess byproducts of the shrine and Glowkin mycelial constructs. Priestess understands ritual attention, offerings, helper coordination and attunement. Preparation may produce catalysts, condensed resources or temporary support effects where materials and rites permit; this does not itself grant a free Power, universal Mana supply, or an unlimited production loop.

!!! Trait Direction

Future picks may support shrine and ritual logistics, illusion and threshold control, support casting, companion coordination, survival by retreat and mycelial/silk field problem solving. Maintain other company niches.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/defenses`>>

!! Defenses

''Quickstart formulas'' (SDM Ch.1 §6): Physical = 7 + Agility + Skill + ''Armor'' ·
Mental = 7 + Thought + Skill + ''Ward'' · Social = 7 + Charisma + Skill + ''Prestige''.

!!! Base — Heritage Only

Counts Aki's own body and nothing she wears.

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Spider Folk Armor 1 | 9 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Spider Folk Ward 1 | 11 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 + Prestige 0 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 1 | 14 |

!!! Base — Heritage + Worn Gear

Counts the Armor and Ward the gear ledger already buys and Aki already wears.

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Armor 3 //(heritage 1 + silksteel robes 2)// | 11 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Ward 5 //(heritage 1 + hat 2 + menpo 1 + netsuke 1)// | 15 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 + Prestige 0 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 5 | 18 |

!!! Open Fork — Which Base Row Governs

<<~ pranala slot=`#defense-source-fork` from=`?` to=`lar:///elyncia.neo-thracia.opens/playtest/defense-source-ruling`>>
''Which base row governs play stays open at the table.'' The two tables differ by 2 Physical
and 4 Mental, so the fork moves every contested roll against Aki. The gear carries canonical
numbers — Ruffle Coat comparator `armor +2`, Moss Hat `ward +2`, Dust Face `ward +1`, Safety
Scarab `ward +1` — and the Quickstart formulas read Armor and Ward without distinguishing worn
sources from bodily ones. Two readings stand:

# ''Gear counts.'' Worn Armor and trinket Wards feed Defense as the formula reads them; the
  second table governs.
# ''Trinkets feed saves only.'' Wards from trinkets grant save bonuses while heritage Ward alone
  reaches Defense; the first table governs.

Reading 2 needs a written FTLS alpha ruling to stand, because the Quickstart text grants Ward
''both'' save bonuses and mental defenses in one sentence. Freyja's and the referee's hand decides;
until then both tables ride, and the sheet names the fork rather than choosing it.

!!! Wearing Ichi

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Damage Threshold | Ichi Level | 2 |
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Ichi/Aki Armor 6 | 14 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Ichi/Aki Ward 2 | 12 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 2 | 15 |

These rows count Ichi's Ward +1 and Aki's heritage Ward +1. The #defense-source-fork reaches
here too: should trinket Wards feed Defense, the hat, menpo, and netsuke add +4 more wherever
Aki still wears them under the armor — and whether she wears a wide-brimmed travel hat inside a
powered symbiote asks its own question. Settle the fork first; this table follows it.

!!! Domain Notes

''Wizard'' may apply against hostile Powers, glamours, illusion warfare, DreamNet intrusion, magical signal attacks, hostile noospheric pressure, and magical analysis contests.

''Alchemist'' may apply to reagents, materials, alchemical transformations, cultivation, extraction, distillation and prepared substance effects.

''Priestess'' may apply to curses, shrine law, offerings, daemon etiquette, ritual contamination, purification, consecration and binding or oath pressure.

''Spider Folk Heritage'' may apply where webs, thread systems, silk structures, climbing, ambush geometry, vibration-reading, or spider-fae social logic matter.


!!! Annotation — Equipment and Symbiosis (OPEN)
The Quickstart's Armor/Ward wording supports the gear-counts reading for worn equipment; the existing alternate defense row remains as a named table fork. Confirm which accessories physically fit and function during Ichi symbiosis before adding their Ward ratings to the Ichi-worn row. Ichi moving to Social Inventory does not itself rewrite their armor, DT, Burn or mode-switch numbers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/inventory`>>

!! Inventory — Current Harness, Field Kits and Shrine Stores (RULING)

''Item slots:'' 7 + Strength 0 = ''7''. Source rule: one sack (sk) = ten stones (st), one stone = ten soaps (sp); an ordinary available item costs at least one slot, and accessing packed gear normally needs an action. The nested carriers below enact an operator-approved playtest exception to separate outer Item slots from named bandolier pocket slots.

!!! Aki's Personal Item Inventory (current ruling)

| Worn / carried equipment | Outer Item slots | Current disposition |
|---|---:|---|
| Silksteel Ritual Miko Robes + Veiled Miko Work Hat + Silk Filter Menpo | 1 | One coherent worn outfit only while kept together; preserve the items' separately recorded effects subject to defense-stacking review |
| Backpack with integrated four-position harness | 2 | One combined two-slot outer carrier, NOT 2+1 for backpack and harness; includes three bandoliers plus one toolbelt |
| Shoulder satchel | 1 (provisional) | Compact field bag; no longer carries the full ten-stone quantum starting kit |
| Naginata | 1 | External/ready polearm; its provenance and final weapon profile remain separately tracked |
| ''Used'' | ''5 / 7'' | No separate outer slot charges for harness, bandolier contents, toolbelt grimoire or toolbelt Thawnettes |
| ''Free'' | ''2 / 7'' | Available for other personal gear; bulk and carrying compatibility still matter |

''Historical source tally (SUPERSEDED):'' The original recorded Spinneret Kit 1 slot, three separately worn robe/hat/menpo slots, two independent Thawnette slots, a full-sack Expedition Satchel counted provisionally as one, and Ichi as a Hallmark. Current rulings move Ichi to Social Inventory, combine the three worn pieces, nest two Thawnettes and the grimoire in the integrated toolbelt, relocate full professional kits to the shrine, and allow only a compact shoulder field satchel.

!!! Backpack's Internal Packed Inventory — 6 one-stone positions

| Position | Prepared subset, not another full quantum kit | Ready state |
|---|---|---|
| BP-01 | Alchemist field subset drawn from shrine-held Alchemist professional kit | Packed; at least one action to retrieve |
| BP-02 | Priestess field subset drawn from shrine-held Priestess professional kit | Packed; at least one action to retrieve |
| BP-03 | Spinneret field subset drawn from shrine-held Spinneret full kit | Packed; at least one action to retrieve |
| BP-04 | EMPTY | Available packed capacity |
| BP-05 | EMPTY | Available packed capacity |
| BP-06 | EMPTY | Available packed capacity |
| ''Used'' | ''3 / 6'' | |
| ''Free'' | ''3 / 6'' | |

''Field subset constraint:'' Each subset occupies one packed stone position. Prepare and replenish these subsets from actual shrine stocks; moving equipment does not clone it. Their precise list of tools, consumables, preparation yields, and any separate acquisition cost remain OPEN. Mess and camping kits have been explicitly removed from this personal loadout.

!!! Integrated Harness Positions (nested management slots, zero extra outer cost)

The backpack's two outer slots ''include'' the harness; its structure does not charge an additional outer slot. Four attachments fit: positions H-1, H-2, H-3 carry one bandolier each, and H-4 carries one toolbelt. Each bandolier has SIX separately accountable pockets; each pocket carries up to FIVE soaps, totaling 3 stones per bandolier. These pocket positions belong ON the character sheet; they must not be counted as personal 1-stone slots a second time.

| Harness position | Contents | Nested pocket positions |
|---|---|---|
| H-1 · Dart bandolier | Twelve prepared chitin rope darts, two per pocket | D-01 through D-06, each 5 sp |
| H-2 · Charm bandolier | Twelve prepared silken omamori charms, two per pocket | O-01 through O-06, each 5 sp |
| H-3 · Alchemical bandolier | Balefire, spore charges, reagents and components as prepared and sized | A-01 through A-06, each 5 sp |
| H-4 · Tool/Sword/Gun belt | T-01: both Silkthorn Thawnettes together in one nested belt item slot; T-02: grimoire; remaining belt positions OPEN | Belt slot limit and size accounting OPEN |

''Bandolier pocket ledger:''

| Pocket number | H-1: rope darts | H-2: charms | H-3: alchemical supply |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 01 | Darts 01–02 | Charms 01–02 | A-01: unassigned (max 5 sp) |
| 02 | Darts 03–04 | Charms 03–04 | A-02: unassigned (max 5 sp) |
| 03 | Darts 05–06 | Charms 05–06 | A-03: unassigned (max 5 sp) |
| 04 | Darts 07–08 | Charms 07–08 | A-04: unassigned (max 5 sp) |
| 05 | Darts 09–10 | Charms 09–10 | A-05: unassigned (max 5 sp) |
| 06 | Darts 11–12 | Charms 11–12 | A-06: unassigned (max 5 sp) |

''Required size check:'' To store two darts or charms in each 5-sp pocket, each complete dart (including its rope trail) or complete charm must fit within 2.5 sp; larger objects use more pocket capacity or fewer items. Do not assume a Balefire grenade fits a 5-sp pocket without a packaged size. The special toolbelt rule nests both Thawnettes in a single belt ''management'' position; their original one-stone-apiece physical bulk does not disappear, and belt load/maximum positions await definition.

''Preparation cost:'' Pocketed objects carry no free extra attacks or automatic Power activations. For rope darts and spell-bearing charms, apply actual recipes, spells known, materials, charge durations and resource expenditure; twelve physical charm positions do not create twelve unpaid spells. Equipped grimoire occupies T-02 without automatically supplying extra spells.

!!! Three Full Kits — Shrine-Held, No Duplication

''RULING:'' The full Alchemist, Priestess and Spinneret professional kits stay at the Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine (including its attached cargo arrangements). Aki takes ONLY prepared field subsets in BP-01 through BP-03; she does not carry three full kits. The shoulder satchel holds a small reserve of ordinary field items, not the former full-sack kit.

''Provenance guard (SOURCE / OPEN):'' The earlier sheet grants one combined Alchemist/Priestess ten-stone quantum starting kit, and separately records a one-stone Spinneret toolkit. It does NOT award three free ten-stone quantum kits. This operator ruling specifies three shrine-held full professional stocks; how the combined original kit splits, whether supplementary stock must be acquired or crafted, and the full Spinneret kit's extended size and provenance remain OPEN. Quantum selection limits do not reset simply by splitting equipment into new containers.

''Readiness and carrying:'' The backpack holds six packed one-stone positions; the three subsets use three. Harness supplies ready pocket positions; retrieval from backpack or satchel follows usual packed-item timing unless explicitly readied. Backpack-integrated harness costs 2 outer slots total. Standalone harness costs 1 outer slot if used without an integrated backpack/rucksack. A future rucksack's own stated slot cost already incorporates its harness rather than stacking surcharge. Check movement, Ichi compatibility, weight/bulk and physical carrying separately: three full kits stored with the shrine do not burden Aki during solo travel.

''Robe pockets:'' The original Silksteel robes retain their 7 sp of separate small-goods space (Bell-Tikker Clicker 1 sp, Safety Netsuke 1 sp, DreamNet Prayer Relay Ofuda x5 with exact per-ofuda bulk OPEN); never conflate these with the 18 bandolier pocket positions.

''Current totals:'' Outer Aki Items 5 / 7 used (2 free); backpack BP 3 / 6 packed (3 free); three bandoliers 18 / 18 pocket positions assigned by role, H-3's six pockets individually unfilled until a prepared manifest assigns items; H-4 carries Thawnettes and grimoire. Full professional kits remain with shrine stores, subject to shrine/wagon cargo placement audit.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/social-inventory`>>

!! Social Inventory — The Maintained Household

''Standing ruling (Freyja + Episkopos):'' Aki maintains Ichi as familiar, squire and aspiring heroic individual, through relationship rather than property. She also tends Ephyra, homunculi and enshrined artifice as a mobile miko and shrine-operator. The shrine holds the Hallmark; the household carries social obligations and the possibility of reciprocity or refusal.

| Relationship | Responsibility / support | Vulnerability |
|---|---|---|
| Ichi | Repair, power, rest, recognition, consent to symbiosis, personal development | Damage, failed upkeep, burnout, conflicting aims; autonomous personhood remains respected |
| Ephyra | Narrow tasks, rites, supplies, re-binding and release | Task-scope limits, decay, loss of connection |
| Fungus Gumi / homunculi | Habitat, material supply, work assignments, care, formation support | Injuries, depleted substrates, interrupted command and upkeep |
| Shrine's Mother Spore daughter-ring | Offerings, maintenance, ritual ecology, environmental care | Node damage, contested home-Glade claim, disrupted web |

''No numeric Social Inventory cap or automatic additional actions'' have yet been adopted. Compatible companion independence and action economies continue under their own sheets and table rulings.

''Model touchstones:'' shrine-keepers, monks and preservers of knowledge in secluded temples; Soulsborne fire/grave keepers and guardians. Their narrative resonance grants no free purchased Power.

''Symbiosis principle:'' maintaining a relationship makes cooperation possible, not guaranteed. The living network can falter from harm, neglect, ritual disruption or disagreement; restoration may require time, material repair, offerings, negotiation or acts of care.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gear-on-body`>>

!! Gear — On Body

''CURRENT RULING (see #/inventory):'' Full Spinneret Kit moves to shrine, prepared subset rides packed in BP-03; Silksteel robes, hat and menpo together consume one outer slot; both Thawnettes and grimoire ride the nested H-4 toolbelt. The inherited table below preserves original item comparators, not their former personal-slot tally.

| Gear | Canon Basis | Rules / Effect |
|---|---|---|
| Spinneret Kit | Spider Folk toolkit | tool edge for silk/web/thread craft |
| Silksteel Ritual Miko Robes | Ruffle Coat comparator | ''armor +2'' (protects as leather), 1 st; pockets hold 7 sp of free inventory |
| Veiled Miko Work Hat / Ichimegasa with Uchikatsugi Veil | Moss Hat | Ward +2; protection vs charms/nausea |
| Silk Filter Menpo | Dust Face | Ward +1; full-face mask vs dust/haze/spores/toxins |
| Bell-Tikker Clicker | Tikker Clicker | detects corrupting energies; bonus vs corruption |
| Silkthorn Thawnette x2 | Thawnette | thrown entangling nets; 1d4; 1 stone each |
| Safety Netsuke | Safety Scarab | Ward +1 trinket |

!!! Hat

The hat uses a wide-brimmed traveling shrine silhouette, not a tall ritual hat. It gives dust, sun, insect, modesty, anonymity, and threshold-focus fiction.


!!! Annotation — Ready-Access Bandolier and Harness (RULING, bulk details OPEN)
The 2-slot backpack includes its own harness, carrying three bandoliers and the toolbelt without additional outer inventory slots. Record all six 5-soap pockets of each bandolier individually on the sheet; the toolbelt holds the grimoire and two Thawnettes sharing one nested belt position. See #/inventory for pocket ledger and exact allocations. Pocket nesting changes accessibility and slot management, not Power costs or physical item mass.

<<~/ahu>>

