* fungal salves
* spore culture jars
* hand broom
* small bells

!!! Strange Item — DreamNet Prayer Relay Ofuda

Five ceramic-paper prayer slips with faint orichalcum traces. Reusable; alchemy clears the last charm script. Fire and acid resistant, DT 5.

Functions:
* temporary ward anchors,
* shrine route markers,
* ley disturbance indicators,
* veil or illusion procedure anchors,
* ritual relay geometry.


!!! Annotation — Three Full Shrine Kits / Three Prepared Subsets (RULING + SOURCE / OPEN)
The operator places full Alchemist, Priestess and Spinneret working kits with the shrine, then prepares a compact subset of each in backpack positions BP-01 through BP-03. The Quickstart grants only one starting 10-stone quantum kit for one Background, and the inherited sheet names one combined Alchemist/Priestess sack plus a separate 1-stone Spinneret toolkit. Additional full professional stock requires identified acquisition, expansion or crafting; it does not materialize as extra free quantum starting kits. The shoulder satchel carries ordinary field supplies, no longer the full sack. Reagent-to-spell-fuel conversion requires its own recipe and cost procedure.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gear-in-shrine`>>

!! Gear — In Shrine

''Operator ruling — three full professional kits stored with the shrine:''

| Full kit | Source / acquisition status | Field issue |
|---|---|---|
| Alchemist professional kit | Split/expand original combined 10-stone quantum kit; supplemental stock procurement OPEN | BP-01: one-stone prepared subset |
| Priestess professional kit | Split/expand original combined 10-stone quantum kit; supplemental stock procurement OPEN | BP-02: one-stone prepared subset |
| Spinneret professional kit | Existing 1-stone Spinneret Kit provides a source basis; any full workshop extension/capacity remains OPEN | BP-03: one-stone prepared subset |

''Logistics:'' These three full stocks stay within the shrine's workshop and/or attached wagon inventory (exact compartment and total cargo allocation OPEN). Material transferred to a field subset remains deducted/checked out of shrine stores until returned or consumed; no duplication, no new free quantum selection pool.

| Gear | Canon Basis | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Ichi Maintenance Sutra Box | Machination Kit | Ichi/Shrine maintenance tools and machine rites |
| Treated Chitin Patch-Stock | Thorned Leather | organic armor-repair material |
| Ichi Armor Repair Work Order | Hardened Armor/Ward mod comparator | material/service access for armor repair |
| Shrine Weather-Seal Materials | Waterproof Armor/Ward mod comparator | shrine/Ichi/cargo waterproofing |
| Ephyra Spore Sacks x4 | Spore Sack | single-use fungal area-control pods |
| Heretech Ofuda x2 | Heretech Scribbles | glitchy ward papers / warning labels |
| Purification Gourd | Water Extractor | moisture extraction / field purification |
| Hard-Silk Leashes x2 | Hard Leash | chitin-silk belay lines / shrine rigging |


!!! Annotation — Workshop and Byproduct Flow (RULING on capability; PROPOSAL on conversion)
The shrine and towed wagon carry the bulk workshop, packed kit, spare reagents, repairs and cultivated outputs. The shrine's companion sheet tracks 9 stone-scale item slots on its own body plus a separate 6-sack towed wagon. Keep allocations and readiness on that sheet as the quartermaster assigns cargo.

Compatible surplus from the shrine, Mother Spore daughter-ring, homunculi and Ichi's Glowkin mycelial golem substrate may serve as ''raw material'' for Alchemist Path-Magic. Any transfer of stored Mana/Life-equivalent credit, temporary ward, ritual catalyst or overcharge reserve needs an identified recipe, amount, shelf life, capacity and upkeep cost. Aki should not extract Ichi's maintenance tissue or the household's survival supplies without accounting for consequences.

